Hello OSF1 NCSA httpd 1.5 experts,

Re: CPU-bound child processes with NCSA httpd 1.5 on OSF1
    -----------------------------------------------------

I have the NCSA httpd 1.5 server running on an OSF1 (Digital Unix V3.2C)
box.  The standalone server starts with 1 parent process and 5 (max 20) 
child processes. 

I noticed that SOMETIMES (NOT ALWAYS) when a c cgi program get called
(e.g. the old imagemap program) or a form with a POST invocation method 
to a C CGI script is accessed, a child process will get CPU-bounded after 
the C program returns the results sucessfully.  Initially, a child 
process will indicate a 99.0% CPU usage, then after a few more program
invocations, 2 child processes will each shows 49.5% CPU usage, then 
3 child processes 33.0% and so on.  The odd thing is that invocation of 
the program does not cause this behaviour every time. 

Is the 1.5 code buggy or the C script or the CPU management of the host 
machine at fault?

Any solutions/hints/ideas will be gratefully received.


