	What you need to do is acquire and install the X Pixmap Library(xpm).
    Look at the files ftp://export.lcs.mit.edu/contrib/libraries/xpm*.  There
    should be a compressed tarfile plus a few other doc files.  When you
    compile it, it will create two library files, one dynamic, and one
    static.  libXpm.a needs to go into /usr/lib, and libXpm.so should probably
    go into /usr/shlib.  There is also an xpm.h file that will need to go into
    /usr/include/X11/xpm.h.

	tvtwm is the virtual window manager that I use, and it's in the same
    boat; it wants xpm.


