ketil@ii.uib.no writes:
>I think I got 
>
>unresolved:
>XXX virtual table
>
>when virtual functions in class XXX were not defined, just declared.

I guess I'll need to add an FAQ entry for this one.  It's a side effect of
g++'s trick to generate only one copy of the virtual table even when
pragma interface/implementation is not used.   The side effect is that if
you forget to define the first virtual function of a class, you won't get
a virtual function table.
