In article <312D9CF2.41C6@ece.utexas.edu>, Dominik Kacprzak <kacprzak@ece.utexas.edu> writes:
|>I use OSF/1 ver3.2.
|>I would like to install fvwm instead standard window manager.
|>Is it possible?

 Once you get the fvwm package, you have just to send the commands:

------------------------ (from README.install)
        xmkmf
        make Makefiles
                (If this command fails or ends in an endless loop,
                 use the shell script MakeMakefiles).
        make all
Monitor the output of the above commands for error messages.

(It is likely that you will need root privilege to write to the
installation directories. If so, become root now)
        make install
        make install.man
------------------------


|>My system starts X after reboot and open login window.

 You start fvwm in your session,
 for instance with the .Xdefaults  line:

DXsession.windowManagerName:    /usr/bin/X11/fvwm


a.c.

 



