Subject: Mixed case names in user names
Date: 1996/02/06
Message-ID: <4f7vmp$7q5@Starbase.NeoSoft.COM>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 138252981
organization: NeoSoft Internet Services +1 713 968 5800
newsgroups: comp.mail.sendmail,comp.unix.osf.misc

About a week ago I posted to these newsgroups explaining that my
Digital Unix (OSF1) system (3.2d) would not deliver mail to mixed
case user ids.  DEC finally figured this out and the answer turns
out to be:

Add the line "OG" which enables resolution via the GECOS field.
This indeed seems to do what I need, since after adding this to
sendmail.cf, even mail to a username in all lower case will correctly
find its way to the mixed case name.

Other users suggested that I add 'u' to the F= flags for the local mailer.
This was indeed missing, but adding this flag did not make a difference.
However, I have left them in and do not know if removing them would hurt
things.  I assume that it would, and won't even waste my time messing
with it.

Thanks to every who replied.  BTW, some users responded that using
mixed case usernames was a bad idea -- and I agree with you.  At this
moment though, I just cannot make a change mid-stream.

Randy
