The window manager in DU3.2 is mwm (Motif Window manager), not olwm
(Open Look window manager). As for a "better" one, I don't know what
you are looking for, but the system also has on it twm (Tom's Window
manager) (/usr/bin/X11/twm). Also available on the net from many sites
is ctwm, cvtwm, and others, some of which provide workspaces. In DU4.0,
the CDE window manager 'dtwm' will be the default.




