We recently purchased a Prolog compiler for our DEC ALPHAS which are running
under OSF/1 V3.2 and are having problems producing executables because of COFF
format errors.
It appears the prolog compiler is producing a slightly older COFF format
version and when this is passed to 'ld' it is rejected. I believe Digital have
changed the COFF format in 3.2 and assume this is the root of the problem. Is
there any 'fix' or options I can send to either 'cc' or 'ld' which will make it
accept the older COFF format.

Joe.




